{
  "format": "corvint-perf-v0/1",
  "profile": {
    "clause": "GPK-V0-016",
    "cutoffClause": "GPK-V0-017",
    "description": "Interleaved preregistered fresh-process performance protocol measured outside both runtimes. This document is the preregistration: it fixes the task corpus, sample counts, warmup count, percentile estimator, validity predicates, and cutover thresholds before any process is spawned, and a run never rewrites it."
  },
  "oracleCommand": "python3 -m corvint_cli",
  "candidatePackage": "./cmd/corvint",
  "preregistration": {
    "registeredAt": "2026-08-28T00:00:00Z",
    "warmupSamples": 5,
    "measuredSamples": 100,
    "percentileEstimator": "nearest-rank",
    "bootstrapResamples": 10000,
    "bootstrapConfidence": 0.95,
    "bootstrapSeed": 20260828,
    "sampleTimeoutMilliseconds": 120000,
    "interleave": "alternating-per-sample"
  },
  "validity": {
    "requireEqualStdout": true,
    "requireEqualStderr": true,
    "requireEqualExitStatus": true,
    "requireCorpusUnchanged": true,
    "requireCacheStableDuringMeasurement": true,
    "forbidTimeouts": true,
    "forbidFailures": true,
    "minimumMeasuredSamples": 100,
    "requirePreregisteredSampleCounts": true,
    "corpusUnchangedNote": "The unchanged-corpus predicate covers what `git status` covers. Git-ignored paths are excluded from the worktree digest per decision 0038 (2026-09-03), because GPK-V0-022 requires repository status before and after each read-only case to be identical and an ignored path never appears in status; the count of excluded paths is recorded as ignoredPaths and never compared. A tracked file its own .gitignore also covers stays covered."
  },
  "thresholds": {
    "nonQueryHarnessP95Milliseconds": 100,
    "portableProductCapMilliseconds": 250,
    "queryP95Milliseconds": 500,
    "nonQueryOracleImprovementFraction": 0.5,
    "otherCommandRegressionFraction": 0.1
  },
  "pluginRowClasses": [
    {
      "class": "adapter-overhead",
      "comparison": "adapter-wall-minus-kernel-wall-for-same-golden-event",
      "bound": {
        "p95Milliseconds": 50,
        "maxMilliseconds": 100,
        "maxExtraCorvintProcesses": 0
      }
    }
  ],
  "corpora": [
    {
      "id": "corvint",
      "repositoryPath": ".",
      "revision": "d995231016b184fc00ea922c9ec8634fb300f0e7",
      "enabled": true,
      "notRunReason": "",
      "indexNote": "This slice compiles its bounded context index in-process per invocation; no persisted index artifact exists. The GPK-V0-017(b) precondition 'after an index is available' is therefore satisfied by a clean authority-bearing corpus plus the five discarded warmups, which settle the content-addressed CORVINT_CACHE_DIR entries both runtimes read."
    },
    {
      "id": "beamfall",
      "repositoryPath": "~/projects/beamfall-workspace/beamfall",
      "revision": "fa3b1e7fe5bc6c10e4b09b2729f364780f567a48",
      "enabled": true,
      "notRunReason": "",
      "indexNote": "This corpus measures the snapshot-miss path: no setup runs before the warmups, so every measured invocation compiles its bounded context index in-process, the same as the corvint corpus. The five discarded warmups settle the content-addressed CORVINT_CACHE_DIR entries both runtimes read. GPK-V0-022 additionally requires that repository status before and after each read-only case be identical, which the runner's own unchanged-repository predicate enforces per measured window."
    },
    {
      "id": "beamfall-snapshot-present",
      "repositoryPath": "~/projects/beamfall-workspace/beamfall",
      "revision": "fa3b1e7fe5bc6c10e4b09b2729f364780f567a48",
      "enabled": true,
      "notRunReason": "",
      "setup": [["index"]],
      "indexNote": "This corpus measures the snapshot-hit path: the candidate runs `corvint index` once against the materialized corpus before the five discarded warmups and the 100 measured samples, outside timing, so a persisted index artifact exists under .corvint/index/ for every measured invocation. The warmups then settle the content-addressed CORVINT_CACHE_DIR entries both runtimes read. GPK-V0-022 additionally requires that repository status before and after each read-only case be identical, which the runner's own unchanged-repository predicate enforces per measured window against the post-setup corpus state."
    }
  ],
